Thanks Henrik,

I uninstalled R, started from scratch, installed as much as I could
from "source" so things compiled locally, and now it works.

As Kasper mentions in the thread you indicate, affxparser works on
Snow Leopard for him but he compiled it locally.  That worked for
me too.  So there appears to be something amiss with the build
provided by Bioconductor.

> require("aroma.affymetrix")

> cdf <- AffymetrixCdfFile$byChipType("GenomeWideSNP_6", tags = "Full")
