Hi Henrik,

In the vignette "http://www.aroma-project.org/node/88", the LRR data were stored under "rawCnData", but it seems to me that in recent updates you have created a new sub-directory called "totalAndFracBData" - what are the difference between these two directories? Which one should I use?

Also in the same vignette, the TotalCnBinary files are named something like "%s,log2ratio,total.asb". I remember seeing somewhere that the "log2ratio" tag is used by aroma to tell what type of data the file contains. If I also created binary files containing BAF data, do I need to keep this tag and simply change "total" to "fracB"?

Thank you very much.

Best,
Kai

